WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.670
-Our first guest tonight is a
Golden Globe-nominated actress

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.538
you know from shows
like "Parks and Recreation,"

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.707
as well as the films
"The Little Hours"

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.509
and "Ingrid Goes West."

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.477
She stars in and produced
"Emily the Criminal,"

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:12.979
which is
streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.114
She also, just this morning,
received

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.283
a Golden Globe nomination
for "The White Lotus,"

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.951
which you can catch on HBO Max.

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:21.821
Please welcome back to the show
our friend Aubrey Plaza,

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.922
everybody.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.923
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.923 --> 00:00:27.927
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:33.433
♪♪

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:38.972
♪♪

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.906
Aubrey, I'm so happy
you're here!

00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:44.310
-I'm happy, too.
-I was always so thrilled

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.278
that we were getting you,
you know,

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:48.915
the night after the
season finale of "White Lotus,"

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:49.983
but then the added bonus --

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.851
you got your Golden Globe
nomination today.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.353
Congratulations.
-I know. What the -- What?

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.688
-I know.
-What? Why?

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.123
-Were you excited?
Was it an exciting thing

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.290
to find out?
-Yeah.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.326
I was completely blown away.
I mean --

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.527
-That's great.
-I couldn't believe it.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.496
-It's so well deserved.
I reached out to you

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.798
midway through the season
because it's so wonderful

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.466
to see you in this part.
It's so great.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.036
And it must have been so --
And I should note,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.004
we are gonna spoil the show.
-Yes.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:13.873
-But everybody should
have watched it when it aired.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.309
You spoiled it for us
by not watching it.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.777
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.379
Did you love
that you knew this thing

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.414
that everybody was so desperate
to find out?

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:24.350
-Um, yeah.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.785
I love having
knowledge and secrets

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:28.321
to hold over everyone.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.889
-You're good with
knowledge and secrets.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.892
-Yeah. Yeah, it's fun.
It's fun.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.127
I was actually surprised

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.529
by how many people
didn't want to know.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.364
It's kind of a litmus test
for people.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.700
It's, like, certain people
want to know,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.602
and it really tells a lot
about a person

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.405
that wants the spoiler
and doesn't care.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.939
-It's true.
-Right?

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:48.140
-One of the great things
about the show is

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.375
there is
this element of mystery.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.344
Obviously, you know
from the first shot

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:55.648
that someone or some people die.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.716
-But the show
is so fun to watch

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.251
that even if it wasn't
this mystery,

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.052
you would love the time
you spent with the characters.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.154
So it's not necessarily
the most important thing.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:05.825
But when you told people,
were they happy?

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.027
Like, when you spoiled it
for people ahead of time,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.930
did you feel joy in their eyes?
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.331
-No. I mean, I don't know.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.767
Like, some people --
People are shady.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.869
Like, some people --
Some people --

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.338
I got some texts
about some Vegas betting.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.374
-Oh, really?
-Some people -- Yeah.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.509
-Some people wanted to
get inside info

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.178
and then go place big money?
-Yeah, yeah,

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.846
there was, like,
insider trading happening.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:30.249
I try to not get involved
in anything illegal.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.952
You know?
But, yeah, I don't know.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.221
Some people --
Yeah, most people don't --

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.723
don't want to know.
But some people

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:38.958
are just like, "Tell me.
I don't care."

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.993
I'm like, "You're sick."
[ Laughter ] =

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.495
And I'll be like,
"She kills all the gays

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.963
and then kills herself
by accident.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.866
Ha! Bye.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.267
I don't know.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.936
Like, that's what happened,
right?

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:51.971
-Yeah, Yeah,
that's what happened.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.207
-Yeah, it's weird.
I don't know,

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.708
it really tells a lot
about a person.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.443
-Was there a character
you wish had died?

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.345
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.746
You don't have to say
if you don't want to.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.616
-I mean, Cameron.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.752
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.987
A lot of people are speculating
because, again,

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.522
we don't ever see what happens
with Harper and Cameron

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:13.526
in the bedroom.
We only hear your side of it.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.894
What do you think
actually happened?

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.128
You, as an actor,
how did you approach it?

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:18.064
-As an actor?

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.999
-Like, as you played
the character...

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.968
-Uh-huh?
-...and the...

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.068
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:24.870
-What?
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.373
-What do you think happens?
I haven't seen the final --

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.775
I haven't seen the edited --
-I believe, Harper.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.577
I believe that they --
-What did I say?

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:34.346
-That they kissed.
-That's what I said?

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:36.248
-Yeah.
-That we kissed?

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.417
-That's what your character
said, yeah.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:40.153
-And what else?
-The way you're looking at me,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.521
like --
-I told you, Seth,

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:45.457
I haven't seen it.
I don't know what goes on --

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:47.493
-You were there.
Stop acting like

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.163
I have an experience
that's unique from yours.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:53.066
I swear to God, it was you.
I watched you.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.800
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.770
-I know what happened, okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.507
And what happened is,
we did some stuff.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.142
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.645
-And I hated every minute of it.
-Okay. Good.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:08.281
-It was disgusting.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:11.417
And there was no penetration.
-Oh, wow.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.419
-I don't know!
-This is very exciting.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.887
-Why?
What do you think happened?

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.889
-Like I said, I believed Harper
that it was just a kiss.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.592
I mean, again, this is --
I mean, I'm trusting you as --

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.594
-Just a kiss?
-Yeah.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.595
You're making me feel
like a dope now

00:04:23.595 --> 00:04:26.833
that I believe your performance.
-No, I just didn't know

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.534
how it was --
-I mean, I think maybe --

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.637
I think maybe each of you
grabbed the other one's butt.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:34.307
[ Laughter ]
Through clothes.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.942
-I think I grabbed
a little more than that.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.510
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.546
What does my husband do?
That's the real question.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.648
-What does your husband --
-Yeah, what does he do

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.317
with, you know, what's-her-face?
-Oh, when they, like,

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.218
sort of stroll off?
-Yeah.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.421
-Yeah. All of a sudden, you're
like, "I haven't seen it,"

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.456
but you know a lot about it.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.759
-I read the scripts.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.126
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.729
-At the end, we see --
-How did they put together?

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:59.098
-Well, now I feel weird
telling you

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.066
about the show you're in.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:04.236
-I'm not -- First of all,
I'm gonna watch it all.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.472
But I want to watch --
I've seen one and two.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:09.208
I want to watch them all, like,
with a very --

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.143
with, like,
a magnum bottle of wine.

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:12.911
-Yeah, that's
a good way to watch it.

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:14.513
-And then I just want to
watch them all

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:16.516
like a movie because, for me,
it's like a seven-hour movie.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:19.385
And it hurts too much.
It's too -- It's like I --

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.155
It's such a slow burn,
I couldn't handle it.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.023
-You mean, when you watched
the first two?

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.524
-When I tried to watch the --
Yeah.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.993
I was like, "I can't do this.
I got to do it in one sitting."

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:31.563
So I'm waiting to do that.
-Now, you do know, at the end,

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:33.966
there's sort of a shot of you --
-What?

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.534
-Harper and Ethan
are at the airport.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.436
-Doing what?
-And they just kind of

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:38.871
look like
they're gonna be okay.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.739
Do you think long-term
they're gonna be okay?

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:43.175
-[ Sighs ]

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:45.378
I mean, I'll just say

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:48.781
that I was really gunning for
doing some takes

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.350
where, like,
maybe we weren't so happy.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.618
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.987
-And I -- I don't know.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.789
Maybe they'll be okay.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:59.491
But I have a kind of fantasy
that Harper divorces him

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.293
and takes all his money.
-Okay, that's a good fantasy.

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.329
And we don't know.
We're all allowed to have

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.930
our own fantasies
about these characters.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.199
-Yeah, I have
a lot of fantasies.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.069
-I have one last thing
to ask you about.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:13.406
-What?
-Your costar Meghann was here.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.840
-Yes.
-She told a story

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.409
about you guys going on a hike
in Sicily,

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.945
and she took responsibility
for the fact

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.246
that you got lost on this hike.

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:23.082
She said she'd done this hike
a bunch on her own,

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:24.917
and the one time
she brought you, she got lost.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.519
But you feel like
she left out a detail.

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.454
-Okay, first of all,
Meghann Fahy is

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.122
an incredible actress.
-She's so wonderful.

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:31.724
-I just want to
give it up to her.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:34.460
Her performance on the show
is sick.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.028
[ Cheers and applause ]
-In the finale, as well.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:38.530
She has a moment in the finale
which is really tremendous.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:42.568
-She slays, even though, like,
character-wise, I'm like,

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.070
"You're trying to
[Bleep] my husband?

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.572
Uh, no."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:49.341
But that's my -- No, she --

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:51.577
Yeah, I saw her on your show
because I watch your show.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.645
And she left out
the most important part,

00:06:53.645 --> 00:06:55.580
which is that we
were on mushrooms.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.416
So first of all...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.416 --> 00:07:00.920
And I don't know if, like,
maybe her parents don't like --

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.488
-Her parents were actually here
that night.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:05.057
-Oh, no. Sorry, Meghann.
-They left with her.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:07.393
Don't worry.
-We took a little one.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.194
-Okay.
-And so,

00:07:09.194 --> 00:07:10.930
when she was telling the
story -- because I watched it.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.098
I'm like, she told the story,

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.865
and it was like,
"Aubrey was on the road,

00:07:13.865 --> 00:07:15.434
and all these Italian guys
are on motorcycles,

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:16.902
and Aubrey was like,
'Don't look at me.'"

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:20.439
I was tripping.
It was terrifying.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.707
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.409
We were lost on a highway,

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:26.478
and there were Italian men going
"Vroom, vroom,"

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:28.113
like, coming at me.
I was like --

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:29.949
I thought they were taking me
to the dark side.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:33.085
Like, I was gonna transfer over.
-She told a story

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.688
that made you seem
rude to Italian motorists.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:39.459
-I was tripping balls, bitch.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:42.995
-She left out
some massive context.

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:44.930
-I know.
-Well...

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.432
-Mushrooms are really good
for depression, though.

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.634
-Oh, that's good, until
you end up on the highway.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.502
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:54.140
-Hey, I also want to ask you
about "Emily the Criminal,"

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.175
which is a fantastic film
that you are starring in

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:57.410
and produced.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.744
We'll be back with more
from Aubrey Plaza.

